$schema: changelog.schema.eure

base = "7a5e2a5143c78c672407b0d98b84868347f905b9"
summary = ````markdown
Borrows are written in the type (`x: &T`) and are values that can be stored; kinds are written `struct(affine)`; library modules have lower-case names and the prelude is split into `std::prelude` and `std::builtin`; arithmetic performs `overflow` and `divzero`; `show` is a function over the class `Debug`; `for` loops, `let` patterns, `ghost fn` and `inductive class` join the language; `HashMap` is a checked library type; `tauto run` asks for permissions at the start; workspaces, an LLVM backend and a run-time ownership checker are added, and the tree evaluator is removed.
````

@ added[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
`borrows(m, x.f)` after a function's result names the parameters the result borrows from: `fn get(m: &HashMap(K, V), k: &K): Option(&V) borrows(m)`.
````
details = ````markdown
Without it the result borrows from every borrowed parameter. It is written after the result and row, before `where`, and is trusted on extern functions.
````

@ added[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
Borrowed structs `struct &T { … }`, `&orig T`, and counted references `&rc T`.
````
details = ````markdown
A type may define what its borrow is as a second struct over the same parameters (`struct &Vec(T) { slots: &Slots(T) }`), with an instance of the prelude class `Lend(T)` (`lend`, `owned`); `lend` and `owned` are inserted where a `&T` or a `T` is expected, and `&T { f, … }` builds and matches it. `&orig T` / `&orig x` is a shared reference to the original value that does not go through `Lend`. `&rc e` moves a value into a reference-counted box of type `&rc T`, which is shared whatever the kind of `T`, is read through a shared borrow, and is never written through.
````

@ added[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
`coerce` fields: `struct Checked { coerce value: Text, length: u64 }` lets `&Checked` be used as `&Text`. `coerce(mut)` also allows `&mut` and field writes, and `coerce(owned)` also the owned value.
````

@ added[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
`let(stack) x := e` places a binding in the function's frame, with no allocation or reference counting. The type must be sized and non-recursive.
````

@ added[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
`pub(handle) effect`: other files may name the effect in rows and handle it, but only the declaring scope performs it.
````

@ added[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
`for x in e { … }` loops over an owned `Iterator`, with `break` and `continue`. The loop is a finite fold, so it adds no `div` to the row.
````
details = ````markdown
`std/finite_iteration.taut` (`FiniteStep`, `IterationControl`, `fold_finite`, `run_finite`, `fold_finite_effectful`) and `std/iterator.taut` (classes `Iterator`, `SharedIterator`, `ExclusiveIterator`, `ListSource`, with instances for `List`) are what the loop is read as. The pattern may destructure.
````

@ added[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
`let` with a pattern: `let #(a, b) := p`, `let Point { x, y } := p`, `let [x, ..rest] := l`. It is the `match` of the value with that one arm, so the pattern must be exhaustive.
````

@ added[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
`ghost fn`: a function only proofs and types use. The kernel reads it as it reads `fn`, extraction never writes it, and executable code that calls it is an error.
````

@ added[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
Trailing commas in parameter, argument, generic, variant, pattern, product, list and constraint lists; row literals that span lines; lambdas and `×` / `->` types as named implicit arguments (`f(<step: (h, w) => next(h, w)>, x)`); `r#` on any path segment (`List::r#type`).
````

@ added[]
area = "types"
summary = ````markdown
Typed arms on a union: `match s { c: Shape => area(c), n: i64 => n }`, with `rest: {Text | Bool} => …` for several members. Exhaustiveness is per member.
````

@ added[]
area = "types"
summary = ````markdown
`uhost`, the unsigned integer of the target's word (32 bits on JavaScript, 64 elsewhere), and the integer types `i8`, `i16` and `u16`.
````
details = ````markdown
`+`, `-`, `*` on `uhost` are the host effects `uhost_add`, `uhost_sub`, `uhost_mul`, and `host_width()` tells the width. `std/uhost.taut` gives the model `UHost` for proofs.
````

@ added[]
area = "classes"
summary = ````markdown
Superclasses (`class Child(A: Type) where Parent(A) { … }`), `where` on a class method, instances for function types (`instance<A, R> Handler((A) -> R)`), `infer from` conditions on an instance, and naming an instance at a call with `C(T)::m(…)`.
````
details = ````markdown
`instance C(A, B) infer from A ∧ B where …` states which known class arguments determine the others. A method need not mention the class parameter (`fn name(): Text`) and is then called as `Named(Circle)::name()`.
````

@ added[]
area = "modules"
summary = ````markdown
An `import` may be written at the head of the body of a top-level `fn`, `macro fn`, `theorem` or `def`; it brings its names into that body only.
````

@ added[]
area = "modules"
summary = ````markdown
Replaceable `extern` blocks: an `extern { … }` whose `struct` / `enum` and `fn` members have Tauto bodies runs those bodies unless host bindings are given for every member of the block.
````
details = ````markdown
Binding only some members is a build error, and the types' representation is sealed to the block. Members without bodies and replaceable members do not share a block.
````

@ added[]
area = "proofs"
summary = ````markdown
`proof!` has sentence forms for connectives and quantifiers: `Let x.`, `Assume h: P.`, `Take x = e.`, `Obtain x and h from e.`, `We show both.`, `We show the left.` / `We show the right.`, `This is impossible by h.`, and `By transitivity of L on h1, h2, ….`.
````
details = ````markdown
`Consider x.` on a variable generalizes the later assumptions whose types depend on `x` and rebinds them in each case under the same names.
````

@ added[]
area = "macros"
summary = ````markdown
Macros can make and read classes and instances: `quote stmts { … }` accepts `class` and `instance`, syntax values have `StClass` and `StInstance`, and a generated-declaration list may name `module`, `effect`, `class` and `instance` (`@keyed!(0) => instance Key`).
````

@ added[]
area = "macros"
summary = ````markdown
A declaration takes several attribute macros, one per line; a typed macro takes a type as its argument (`json_schema!(Forecast)`); a macro declared under a path is called by that path (`M::NAME!(…)`).
````
details = ````markdown
New functions of the macro API: `Elab::data`, `Elab::class_decl`, `Elab::implicit_names`, `Elab::call`, `Judgement::generics` and `Syn::product_items`. Float literals are syntax values (`ExFloat`).
````

@ added[]
area = "macros"
summary = ````markdown
Grammars of `syntax!` and `inductive_syntax!` name several start symbols with `%start A, B, …`, and an `inductive_syntax!` may hold holes (`Value: Num | Hole;` with `Hole: TautoExpr;`).
````
details = ````markdown
`tauto syntax gen` writes the tables of another start symbol `B` to `<sha256>.B.tables`. More expressions are read after a bare `$` in a DSL: paths (`$Nat::add(n, 0)`), tuples (`$#(a, b)`) and macro calls taking a backtick literal.
````

@ added[]
area = "macros"
summary = ````markdown
The built-in `include_bytes!("path")` embeds a file as `Bytes`, and `include_text!` / `include_bytes!` may read the directories that the manifest lists in `package.include-from`.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
The class `Debug` with `debug(&a): Text` (`std/prelude/debug.taut`). Every `struct`, `enum` and `inductive` has an instance: the one its file writes, or one the compiler writes.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
`std/key.taut`: the class `Key(K)` (`eq`, `feed`, with laws) and the macro `keyed!` that derives the instance of a struct from its fields. `std/hash.taut`: SipHash-1-3. `std/indexed_map.taut`: `IndexedMap(K, V)`, a hash map that walks in insertion order.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Slot storage and the containers built on it: the prelude type `Slots`, `std/slots.taut`, `std/slots_store.taut`, `std/vec.taut` (`VecModel`) and `std/hash_table.taut`, with their proofs.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Regions and allocators: `std/builtin/region.taut` (`Region`, `Place`, `Placed` and their counted forms), `std/alloc.taut` (the class `Policy` with the proved `BumpPolicy` and `PoolPolicy`), `std/bump.taut` and `std/pool.taut`.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
`std/template.taut`: the `text!` macro (``text!(`Hello, $name! ${n + 1}`)``) and formatters such as `pad_start`, `hex`, `bin`, `grouped` and `quoted`.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
`std/sse.taut`: a decoder of server-sent events with the theorem that feeding pieces equals feeding their concatenation. `std/os.taut`: proofs can read functions that perform or handle the standard effects.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Host effects in `std::builtin::os`: streaming HTTP (`net_open`, `net_write`, `net_finish`, `net_cancel`, `net_read`, `net_close`), `fs_set_mode`, `fs_lock` / `fs_unlock`, `timer`, `environ`, `hash_seed` and `host_width`; path helpers `path_parent`, `path_name`, `path_join`.
````
details = ````markdown
`FileStat` has the field `executable`, so a handler of `fs_stat` that builds a `FileStat` gives it.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Waiting with a deadline in `std::builtin::par`: `wait_until`, `Task::join_until`, `Mutex::take_until`, `Semaphore::acquire_until` and `Channel::recv_until`.
````

@ added[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Prelude functions `map_ref`, `each_ref`, `fold_ref`, `Array::set`, `Bytes::find`, `U64::of_text`, `U64::wrapping_add` / `sub` / `mul`, `Text::replace_all`, `Text::index_from` and `Text::occurs_at`, with lemmas for `Array::set` and `Bytes::find` in `std/array.taut` and `std/bytes.taut`.
````

@ added[]
area = "meta"
summary = ````markdown
Axiom-free models of mutable state in `meta/mutable_*.taut` (`docs/design/mutable-state-model.md`), and `meta/latent_rows.taut` for the effects of a spawned body.
````

@ added[]
area = "lean"
summary = ````markdown
The Lean kernel model covers numerals and `+`, `*`, `-` on `Nat` (`lean/Proto/Kernel/Literals.lean`), and the Nib model proves that a freeze ends at the last use of its holder (`lean/Proto/Nib/LastUse.lean`) and that an effect whose answer holds a borrow keeps loans free of conflicts (`lean/Proto/Nib/EffectLend.lean`).
````

@ added[]
area = "manifest"
summary = ````markdown
Workspaces: a root lists member totes (`workspace { members = ["engine", glob`plugins/*`] }`), each member names its root (`workspace = ".."`), and members depend on each other by package name (`engine: workspace`).
````
details = ````markdown
A manifest without `package` is a virtual root. The project lock is the `Tauto.lock` beside the outermost root. `tauto check` at a workspace root checks every member. Design: `docs/design/workspace.md`.
````

@ added[]
area = "manifest"
summary = ````markdown
`trust.run` lists the permissions a project grants its own runs, narrowed to paths, names or hosts; `test { retries = N }`; `package.entry` names the file whose top level runs; `rust.main-thread` runs `main` on the process's main thread; `sparse = true` on a Git dependency with `dir` fetches and hashes only that directory.
````

@ added[]
area = "cli"
summary = ````markdown
`tauto build --backend llvm [--emit llvm|nir] [--export ENTRY]... [-o FILE]` builds a native program through LLVM and `clang`.
````
details = ````markdown
On Linux x86_64 the program stands on system calls and links no library; elsewhere it uses only the C library's entry points to the OS. A program that uses something the backend does not write (`Float`, unions, `linear` types, resuming or aborting handlers, host-bound `extern`s) is refused whole with a message naming it. Design: `docs/design/llvm-backend.md`.
````

@ added[]
area = "cli"
summary = ````markdown
`tauto run --backend niri FILE` runs the program on an interpreter that checks ownership at run time: it stops at a value used after a move, dropped twice or never dropped, and at a borrow used after its owner is gone.
````

@ added[]
area = "cli"
summary = ````markdown
`tauto run` of an unchanged tote reuses the machine's bytecode and the generated crate, and tactic results of proof steps are cached; cached proof results still go through the kernel. `tauto build --verify` re-verifies the locked dependencies before building.
````

@ added[]
area = "cli"
summary = ````markdown
`tauto check` reports struct fields that are never read (`warning[unused_field]`).
````

@ added[]
area = "lsp"
summary = ````markdown
Language server: a quick fix that writes the `import` for a name used without importing it, a quick fix at `!?` that writes the row, hover on a name in a macro's `=> …` list, and completion of signs by their Unicode character names after a backslash.
````

@ added[]
area = "backends"
summary = ````markdown
NIR has a text form and static checks (`docs/design/nir-text.md`, `docs/design/nir-wf.md`); `tauto build --backend llvm --emit nir` writes it.
````

@ added[]
area = "backends"
summary = ````markdown
Rust backend: regions (`Region`, `Place`, `Placed`) with a bump allocator; `tauto-embed`'s `Tote::try_call` returns `Failure::Exit(code)` or `Failure::Error(message)` instead of ending the host process; a tote keeps its Cargo lock in `Tauto.Cargo.lock` when a `Cargo.toml` of another crate sits beside `Tauto.eure`.
````

@ added[]
area = "totes"
summary = ````markdown
`totes/eure` (a reader, writer and shape checker for Eure documents, with a proved round trip), `totes/sha256`, `totes/totebag-io` (the part of Totebag that touches files), `totes/identity` and `totes/fuzz` (a generator of random well-typed programs).
````

@ added[]
area = "totes"
summary = ````markdown
More of the compiler is written in Tauto: `totes/parse`, `totes/analyzer`, `totes/extract`, `totes/build`, `totes/nir`, `totes/lower`, `totes/niri`, `totes/llvm`, `totes/jsgen`, `totes/synrun` and `totes/synread`.
````

@ added[]
area = "totes"
summary = ````markdown
`totes/unicode`: NFC normalization (`unicode_nfc`, `unicode_is_nfc`), lower-casing (`unicode_lowercase`) and the `XID_Continue` table. `totes/text`: `text_code_points` and `text_parse_i128`.
````

@ added[]
area = "examples"
summary = ````markdown
`examples/user-data-structures/` (models of a growable array and a hash table with their theorems), `examples/borrow-proofs.taut`, `examples/extern-fallback-*`, and the Rust examples `main-thread`, `dependency-bridge` and `bridge-name-collision`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
Borrowed parameters and bindings are written in the type: `x: &T`, `x: &mut T`, `let x := first(&v)`. The binder forms `&x: T`, `&mut x: T`, `let &x := …` and `var &it := …` are gone.
````
details = ````markdown
Whether a `let` borrows is read from the type of its value. This applies to functions, closures (`(q: &P) => q.a`), class methods and extern signatures.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Move the `&` / `&mut` from the name to the type in every parameter (`fn size(&p: P)` becomes `fn size(p: &P)`), and drop it from `let &x :=` / `var &x :=`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
Writing through a `&mut` borrow is `*x := v` (and `*p.r := v` for a borrow held in a field). A field write through `p: &mut Person` stays `p.name := e`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Rewrite assignments to a `&mut` parameter or binding from `x := e` to `*x := e`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "ownership"
summary = ````markdown
Borrows are values that can be stored, and a freeze ends at the holder's last use instead of the end of the block.
````
details = ````markdown
`&p` / `&mut p` may stand as a struct field, a `:=` right side, a `match` scrutinee, a generic argument and an element of a container, and a type argument may hold a borrow (`Vec(&F)`, `Option(&V)`). A type parameter bounded with `NoBorrow` refuses borrow-holding arguments. Borrows still cannot be effect arguments or be captured by an escaping closure.
````

@ changed[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
A kind is written in parentheses after the keyword: `struct(affine) File {}`, `enum(linear) Handshake { … }`, `type(affine) Regex`. The `view` kind is gone: an extern type that holds a borrow is `type(borrow) Iter(A: Type)`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Rewrite `KIND struct|enum|type Name` as `struct(KIND)|enum(KIND)|type(KIND) Name`, and `view struct Iter(A) {}` in an `extern` block as `type(borrow) Iter(A: Type)`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
A lone `_` is a wildcard only in patterns, and `^name` asserts that a binding is unused: `let ^x := e`, `(^x: T) => …`, `fn f<^A>(…)`, `Some(^x)`.
````
details = ````markdown
`^` suppresses the unused warning when the binding is unused and is an error (`unused_marker_used`) when it is used; it is not part of the name. A leading `_` in a name no longer suppresses unused warnings.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Give each `_` binding a name and mark it: `let _ := e` becomes `let ^x := e`. Replace `_name` used to silence a warning with `^name`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
A `match` takes its result type from where it stands (a declaration's body, an arm's body, an annotated `let`, an argument whose parameter type is fixed), so `⊢ T from` is written only where no type is expected or a different goal is needed.
````

@ changed[]
area = "syntax"
summary = ````markdown
`for`, `in`, `ghost`, `coerce`, `infer`, `borrows`, `orig` and `borrow` are reserved words. Identifiers follow Unicode `XID_Start` / `XID_Continue`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Write a name spelled like one of these as `r#name` (`r#in`, `t.r#for`).
````

@ changed[]
area = "types"
summary = ````markdown
A product is written only as `A × B` and `#(a, b)`; the prelude's `Pair` cannot be named. Members are taken by `#(…)`, by the type of a member, or by `.fst` / `.snd`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Replace `Pair(A, B)` with `A × B`, and `Pair { fst: a, snd: b }` in values and patterns with `#(a, b)`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
A `fn` with a body and no row written has the empty row; its row is no longer taken from the body. `fn f(): T !?` asks for the row to be written: `tauto check` reports the row the body performs, and `tauto check --fix` and `tauto lint --fix` write it in place of `!?`.
````
details = ````markdown
An effect written in a row that the body never performs is `warning[unused_effect]`; `^name` in the row (`! { ^Host }`) asserts that it is unused. `tauto lint` rejects `!?` in the files it checks.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Write the row on every function that performs effects, `div`, `overflow` and `divzero` included. Put `!?` after the result and run `tauto check --fix` to have the rows written.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
Built-in effects are lower case (`div`, `divzero`, `exceeded`), and arithmetic that has no result performs an effect: `+`, `-`, `*` on a fixed-width integer whose result does not fit perform `overflow`, and division by zero performs `divzero`.
````
details = ````markdown
Both are declared in `std::prelude::num`, appear in rows and can be answered by a `handle`. Unanswered, the host stops the program with `the number is too large` or `division by zero`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Rename `Div` / `DivZero` / `Exceeded` in rows and arms, and add `overflow` (and `divzero`) to the rows of functions that use these operators, or use the `checked_*`, `wrapping_*` and proof-carrying forms.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
A run-time budget is the host operation `perform budget(n, () => { body })`, with `perform budget_memory(n, f)` for memory. A function that runs a budget has `budget` in its row.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Rewrite `budget(steps: n) { body }` as `perform budget(n, () => { body })` and `budget(memory: n) { body }` as `perform budget_memory(n, () => { body })`, and add `budget` / `budget_memory` to the rows.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
`show` is a prelude function over the class `Debug`: `show(&v)` writes the `Debug` text of a value and a line break to `stdout`. `Show` is the effect set `{ stdout, stdout_flush }`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Replace `perform show(name, v)` with `show(&v)` and the row entry `show` with `Show`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
Entries of a program are the prelude effects `main(body)` and `test(name, body)`: a program writes `perform main(() => { … })`. `test` has a fixed row, and `run_test` is removed.
````
details = ````markdown
A test body may perform `check(path)` to get the `List(Diagnostic)` that `tauto check` gives for a file.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Remove calls to `run_test`; a test body that performed other effects handles them inside the body.
````

@ changed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
Shared state is made and used through effects: `ref_new`, `ref_get`, `ref_set`, `weak_of`, `weak_get`, `mutex_new`, `mutex_put`, `atomic_new`, `atomic_load`, `atomic_store`, `atomic_fetch_add`. `Ref::new`, `Ref::get`, `Ref::set`, `Mutex::new` and `Atomic::*` are no longer callable.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
`Ref::new(v)` becomes `perform ref_new(v)`, `Ref::get(r)` becomes `perform ref_get(r)`, `Mutex::new(v)` becomes `perform mutex_new(v)`, `Atomic::fetch_add(a, n)` becomes `perform atomic_fetch_add(a, n)`; add the effects to the rows of the functions that do so.
````

@ changed[]
area = "classes"
summary = ````markdown
`inductive class` is the class of the proof language; a plain `class` is a program class without laws. The structural predicate `Hash` is removed: maps take their keys by the class `Key`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Write `inductive class` for every class that has `theorem` laws or is used in proofs. Replace `where DecEq(K), Hash(K)` with `where Key(K)` and give key types a `Key` instance.
````

@ changed[]
area = "modules"
summary = ````markdown
A member of `module m { … }` without `pub` is seen only inside the module; `pub module` exposes its public members to importing files, and `pub import M { name }` re-exports a member. A `macro fn` and a function of an `extern` block are seen from other files only when written `pub`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Add `pub` to module members, `macro fn`s and extern functions that other files or the outside of the module use, and write `pub module` for modules other files name.
````

@ changed[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Every library file has a lower-case `snake_case` name, so every import path changed: `std::Nat` is `std::nat`, `std::MapLaws` is `std::map_laws`, `std::proof::Lang` is `std::proof::lang`. The same holds for `meta/`, `examples/`, `totes/algebra` and `totes/whale`. The lint `file-name` reports a `.taut` file whose name has a capital letter.
````
details = ````markdown
The declarations inside keep their names (`Nat::add_comm`, `Ordmap::insert`).
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
Rewrite each import path to the lower-case file name: `import std::Nat { Nat }` becomes `import std::nat { Nat }`, `import std::IntOrder {…}` becomes `import std::int_order {…}`, and `"../std/Base.taut"` becomes `"../std/base.taut"`.
````

@ changed[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
The prelude is split into `std::prelude` (data and functions: `std`, `collections`, `num`, `text`, `debug`) and `std::builtin` (what the host and the compiler provide: `os`, `par`, `macro`, `secret`, `ord`, `classes`, `region`). `std::prelude::Affine` and `std::prelude::Shared` are merged into `std::prelude::collections`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
`import std::prelude::Os {…}` becomes `import std::builtin::os {…}`, and likewise for `Par`, `Macro`, `Secret`, `Ord` and `Classes`. Import `concat` from `std::prelude::std` and `Vec`, `Buf`, `Array`, `Bytes`, `Map` from `std::prelude::collections` where an import is needed.
````

@ changed[]
area = "std"
summary = ````markdown
Fixed-width integers of the proofs are two indexed families, `UInt(w)` (`std/uint.taut`) and `SInt(w)` (`std/sint.taut`), at widths 8, 16, 32 and 64. They replace the separate types `U8`, `U32`, `U64`, `I32` and `I64`, and functions carry the width in their name: `U64::add` is `UInt::add64`, `I64::checked_tdiv` is `SInt::checked_tdiv64`.
````
breaking = true
migration = ````markdown
